ro solution of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}\\cdot {p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}\\cdot {p}_{3}(t)=0.$" 13194139535121 true] [17592186332193 1113 #uuid "2dab8886-dbcc-502c-b885-95f6e15041d6" 13194139535121 true] [17592186332193 1145 "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ not all zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=0.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the given expressions for ${p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),$ and ${p}_{3}(t)$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(1+t+2{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(-2+3t+{t}^{2})+{x}_{3}(3t+3{t}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ ({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})+({x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3})t+(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}){t}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final equation is true for every $t$ if and only if \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding augmented matrix and reduce it to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd. Hence, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable.\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{3}{5}{x}_{3}.$ Substitute it into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(-\\frac{3}{5}{x}_{3})=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-\\frac{6}{5}{x}_{3}.